  "name": "Masaki Evolution Communication Campaign",
  "category": "campaign",
  "description": {
    "text": "Media Factory's Evolution Communication Campaign gave the five \"Masaki promos\", cosmos holo cards of Pokémon that evolve by trading. Vending Series 3, the vending machine sheets released from 24 November 1998, included a pass card called Bill's PC (Masaki's PC in Japanese, Masaki being Bill's Japanese name). Mailing it to Media Factory with a Kadabra, Haunter, Graveler or Machoke card brought back Alakazam, Gengar, Golem or Machamp, a nod to the Game Boy games, where those four evolve only when traded; an Omanyte brought back Omastar, the one of the five that doesn't evolve by trading in the games.\n\nThe campaign closed on 30 April 1999. Media Factory later reported in Trainers Magazine Vol. 2 that over 140,000 people took part, and that it sent out 39,000 Alakazam, 36,000 Gengar, 29,000 Machamp, 22,000 Golem and 21,000 Omastar. The cards came back held by their corners in a card mount printed with a thank-you letter, so many have dented corners.",
